    expectedAnswer: "Design tokens are named values for shared design decisions such as color, spacing, typography, radius, shadow, and motion. They provide a stable semantic layer so components do not need to hard-code raw visual values.",
    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Understand the component-library concept.\n\nStep 1 — Define semantic tokens instead of scattering raw values.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\ninterface DesignTokens {\n  colorPrimary: string;\n  colorText: string;\n  spaceMd: string;\n  radiusSm: string;\n}\n\nconst tokens: DesignTokens = {\n  colorPrimary: \"#2563eb\",\n  colorText: \"#111827\",\n  spaceMd: \"16px\",\n  radiusSm: \"6px\",\n};\n\nfunction buttonStyle(\n  design: DesignTokens,\n): string {\n  return [\n    `background:${design.colorPrimary}`,\n    `color:${design.colorText}`,\n    `padding:${design.spaceMd}`,\n    `border-radius:${design.radiusSm}`,\n  ].join(\";\");\n}\n\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN / CSS-variable mapping:\n```ts\ninterface DesignTokens {\n  colorPrimary: string;\n  colorText: string;\n  spaceMd: string;\n  radiusSm: string;\n}\n\nfunction toCssVariables(\n  design: DesignTokens,\n): Record<string, string> {\n  return {\n    \"--color-primary\": design.colorPrimary,\n    \"--color-text\": design.colorText,\n    \"--space-md\": design.spaceMd,\n    \"--radius-sm\": design.radiusSm,\n  };\n}\n```\n\nExample:\nA `Button` reads `--color-primary` rather than storing a hard-coded blue. A theme can replace the token set without rewriting every component.\n\nComplexity:\nToken lookup is O(1) for direct property access.\n\nTrade-off:\nTokens improve consistency and themeability, but too many tokens can create naming and governance overhead.\n\nStep 5 — Senior interview takeaway:\nExplain the public contract, consumer impact, accessibility/performance implications, and why the chosen abstraction is justified.",
